How it works:

Route 53 resolves the application's domain name.
The Application Load Balancer distributes traffic across EC2 instances in multiple Availability Zones.
EC2 instances handle application logic.
The primary RDS instance stores application data.
Multi-AZ keeps a synchronously updated standby ready for automatic failover.
